<title>USA: Chemfab gets $2.4 mln U.S. Army order.</title>
<headline>Chemfab gets $2.4 mln U.S. Army order.</headline>
<dateline>MERRIMACK, N.H. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemfab Corp said on Tuesday it received a $2.4 million order to supply 32 fabricated chemical warfare protective shelters under a contract recently awarded by the U.S. Army.</p>
<p>The company said delivery of the units is scheduled to start in the current fiscal year and be completed by June 1998.</p>
<p>The planned procurement includes 308 shelter units produced over the next four to five years.  If they all were ordered, the total contract value to Chemfab would be about $20 million, the company said.</p>
</text>
